    "earnings_release": "8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L1: EX-99.1\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L2: 2\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L3: a8-kex991q4202609262026.htm\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L4: EX-99.1\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L5: Document\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L6: Exhibit 99.1\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L7: Apple reports fourth quarter results\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L8: September quarter records for total company revenue, iPhone revenue, and EPS\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L9: Services revenue reaches new all-time high\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L10: CUPERTINO, CALIFORNIA \u2014 Apple\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L11: \u00ae\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L12: today announced financial results for its fiscal 2026 fourth quarter ended September 26, 2026. The Company posted quarterly revenue of $114.5 billion, up 12 percent year over year. Company gross margin was 47.9 percent, including a favorable impact of approximately 1 percentage point from tariff refunds. Diluted earnings per share was $2.10, up 14 percent year over year, and included a favorable impact of $0.05 from tariff refunds.\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L13: \u201cToday, Apple is proud to report a September quarter revenue record of $114.5 billion, up 12 percent from a year ago, with iPhone reaching a September quarter record and Services reaching an all-time high, capping off our best fiscal year ever,\u201d said John Ternus, Apple\u2019s CEO. \u201cWe\u2019re closing the year with our most ambitious lineup yet. That includes the iPhone Duo, the most transformational iPhone since the original, alongside iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max, our most powerful iPhones yet. We also just introduced a whole new generation of hardware for the home and brought Touch to Mac for the first time. Together with the all-new Siri AI, it\u2019s an incredible lineup to carry us into the holiday season.\u201d\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L14: \u201cApple delivered September quarter records for net income and EPS. Our record September quarter capped off a strong fiscal 2026, with all-time record revenue of $479 billion and double-digit EPS growth,\u201d said Kevan Parekh, Apple\u2019s CFO. \u201cWe generated $28 billion in operating cash flow during the quarter, allowing us to return $28 billion to shareholders. Thanks to our very high levels of customer satisfaction and loyalty, our installed base of active devices reached a new all-time high across all major product categories and geographic segments.\u201d\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L15: Apple\u2019s board of directors has declared a cash dividend of $0.27 per share of the Company\u2019s common stock. The dividend is payable on November 16, 2026, to shareholders of record as of the close of business on November 12, 2026.\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L16: Apple will provide live streaming of its Q4 2026 financial results conference call beginning at 2:00 p.m. PT on November 2, 2026, at apple.com/investor/earnings-call. The webcast will be available for replay for approximately two weeks thereafter.\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L17: Apple periodically provides information for investors on its corporate website, apple.com, and its investor relations website, investor.apple.com. This includes press releases and other information about financial performance, reports filed or furnished with the SEC, information on corporate governance, and details related to its annual meeting of shareholders.\n[Evidence omitted from this role packet because of the model context limit.]\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L362: Operating activities:\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L363: Net income\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L364: 132,175\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L365: 112,010\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L366: Adjustments to reconcile net income to cash generated by operating activities:\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L367: Depreciation and amortization\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L368: 13,423\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L369: 11,698\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L370: Share-based compensation expense\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L371: 13,789\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L372: 12,863\n8-K_exhibit_99_1.txt:L373: Other\n8-K_exh